under the DubLine Source License 1.0 unless explicitly stated otherwise.

This transition is defined by the introducing repository revision, not by a
version number, release date, or tag. It does not revoke or restrict rights
already granted under the MIT License for earlier versions and revisions,
including code obtained from those revisions. The historical MIT text is
preserved in LICENSE-MIT-LEGACY for reference only; its inclusion does not
dual-license the current revision. See the License section of README.md for
the recorded transition commit once available.

This is a source-available license. It is not an OSI-approved open-source
license and does not grant unrestricted commercial rights.

