6. Unofficial builds, names, and branding

All third-party executable builds distributed or provided to others, whether
modified or unmodified, must use a product name different from DubLine. This
includes their application name, executable name, package identity, and
distribution listing. They must prominently identify themselves as unofficial
and must not claim or imply that they are official DubLine, endorsed by
Licensor, or produced by Licensor. A private build used only by its builder
need not be renamed.

Source forks must clearly identify themselves as unofficial. You must not
present a fork as the official DubLine project.

The DubLine name, logo, icons, trademarks, and other brand assets are not
licensed with the code. No trademark or brand license is granted. Third-party
builds must replace DubLine logos, icons, and other branding unless Licensor
has given separate written permission. Truthful references to DubLine as the
origin of the code and preservation of required attribution notices are
allowed; they must not imply endorsement.

